NOETHER'S THEOREM (1918) - Emmy Noether

A continuous symmetry of the action
implies a conserved quantity.

Q = Σ_α  p_α (ξ_α − q̇_α τ) + L τ + F

VARIABLES
Q     conserved charge (Noether charge)
p_α   canonical momenta  p_α = ∂L/∂q̇_α
q_α   generalized coordinates
q̇_α   generalized velocities
ξ_α   infinitesimal generators of the
      coordinate transformation
τ     infinitesimal generator of time shift
L     Lagrangian
F     possible total time-derivative term
      (does not change the equations of motion)

FUNDAMENTALS
Time-translation invariance (τ ≠ 0, ξ = 0)
      → energy conservation

Spatial-translation invariance (ξ constant, τ = 0)
      → linear-momentum conservation

Rotational invariance
      → angular-momentum conservation

The action S = ∫ L dt is unchanged
(up to a total derivative) under the
infinitesimal transformation generated
by ξ and τ. The associated Q is then
constant along solutions of the
Euler-Lagrange equations.
